&lt;h1&gt;Your Mission&lt;/h1&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As Senior Customer Success Manager, your mission is to take strategic ownership of a portfolio of enterprise customers and act as a trusted advisor to senior stakeholders across the manufacturing industry. You will drive long-term value realization, retention, expansion, and customer advocacy while helping shape how SPARETECH scales Customer Success across our growing customer base.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h1&gt;&lt;strong&gt;We offer you the opportunity to&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h1&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Own Strategic Customer Outcomes&lt;/strong&gt;: Take end-to-end ownership of a portfolio of enterprise customers, from handover and onboarding to adoption, executive alignment, renewals, expansion, and long-term value realization.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Act as a Trusted Advisor&lt;/strong&gt;: Build strong relationships with senior stakeholders and decision-makers, helping customers translate their business priorities into measurable success with SPARETECH.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Drive Retention and Expansion&lt;/strong&gt;: Identify risks and growth opportunities early, lead proactive success planning, and contribute directly to strong retention, low churn, and sustainable account growth.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Represent SPARETECH Externally&lt;/strong&gt;: Represent us in strategic customer meetings, customer events, webinars, roundtables, and our own regional meetups.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Lead by Example&lt;/strong&gt;: Fully dedicate yourself to self-leadership, driving your personal and professional development while strengthening each each colleague in the team.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Shape How We Scale Customer Success&lt;/strong&gt;: Partner with the VP Customer Success, Product, Sales, and the wider CS team to enhance customer journeys, influence product feedback loops, and build scalable CS practices.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h1&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Become a part of our team if you&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h1&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Bring Senior CS Experience&lt;/strong&gt;: Have 4-7 years of Customer Success experience in B2B SaaS, ideally with enterprise customers in complex, technical, or manufacturing-related environments. You understand process design, CS models, customer segmentation, retention levers, expansion motions, and how to drive measurable customer value in a high-growth SaaS environment.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Think Strategically and Commercially&lt;/strong&gt;: Can independently manage a complex customer portfolio, prioritize effectively, identify risks and opportunities, and drive initiatives across different stakeholder groups.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Build Executive Relationships&lt;/strong&gt;: Connect confidently with key decision-makers and executive sponsors, run strategic conversations, and are willing to travel 2-4 times per month to strengthen customer partnerships and build a vital customer community in the DACH region.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Bring Technical and Industry Curiosity&lt;/strong&gt;: You build up deep product and manufacturing knowledge, thrive on technical challenges, proactively resolve client issues, optimize product adoption, and ensure seamless integration to drive customer satisfaction and retention.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Understand Manufacturing&lt;/strong&gt;: Have firsthand experience with manufacturing processes and know the manufacturing industry from the inside.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Speak Fluently&lt;/strong&gt;: Are proficient in both German and English.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h1&gt;&lt;strong&gt;You can expect&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h1&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A remote-yes company, where you can decide every day whether you work from home, at our Stuttgart or Munich office, or at any&amp;nbsp;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.designoffices.de/&quot;&gt;Design Office&lt;/a&gt; in Germany.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A permanent employment contract, 30 days of vacation, and the opportunity to participate in the company&#39;s success through our VSOP program.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Modern hardware and the frame for a height-adjustable desk.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;An annual training budget of 1000 EURO for your professional development.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;In Germany: A subsidized&amp;nbsp;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.jobrad.org/&quot;&gt;job bike&lt;/a&gt;&amp;nbsp;to escape city traffic and a&amp;nbsp;&lt;a href=&quot;https://qualitrain.net/&quot;&gt;Wellpass&lt;/a&gt; gym membership to stay active.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A dynamic start-up atmosphere and an international team in which new ideas, creative approaches, and cooperation at eye level are valued.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;To enjoy &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.corporate-benefits.de/&quot;&gt;Corporate Benefits&lt;/a&gt;, including discounts on fashion, travel, and much more from various companies.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;h1&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About SPARETECH&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h1&gt;
&lt;p&gt;SPARETECH&#39;s vision is to empower the zero-waste industrial sharing economy by enabling maintenance and procurement teams at manufacturing leaders like Bosch, Porsche, and Nestlé to reduce MRO spend and optimize inventory through accurate part information, internal transparency, and market visibility.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;To achieve this, we have built, and continue to build, an AI-powered MRO software that connects all players in the spare parts ecosystem, from manufacturers and suppliers to the people working behind the machines. By facilitating the exchange of data, knowledge, and expertise, we create shared visibility that empowers smarter decisions, reduces waste, and drives seamless collaboration. This connected spare parts intelligence unlocks value that extends far beyond software.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Backed by&amp;nbsp;&lt;a class=&quot;notion-link-token notion-focusable-token notion-enable-hover&quot; href=&quot;https://www.thesaasnews.com/news/sparetech-raises-10-million-in-series-a&quot; data-token-index=&quot;1&quot;&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;link-annotation-unknown-block-id-1257119756&quot;&gt;Insight Partners&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/a&gt;, SPARETECH is accelerating its growth with a strong focus on product innovation and team excellence. We take pride in our inclusive and collaborative culture, as well as our energetic and committed team.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;Find more English Speaking Jobs in Germany on Arbeitnow

&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p class=&quot;sc-gEkIjz cjtSrT MuiTypography-root MuiTypography-body1 sc-hoLEA&quot;&gt;Raisin is the world’s leading platform for savings and investment products. Founded in 2012, the&amp;nbsp;&lt;strong&gt;FinTech&lt;/strong&gt; connects consumers with banks in the EU, the UK and the US. This gives consumers &lt;strong&gt;better interest rates&lt;/strong&gt; and banks a &lt;strong&gt;diversified form of refinancing&lt;/strong&gt;. Our vision is to offer savings and investments without barriers and thus open up the global 160 trillion euro market.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p class=&quot;sc-gEkIjz cjtSrT MuiTypography-root MuiTypography-body1 sc-hoLEA&quot;&gt;Raisin currently employs more than 800 people from over 75 countries worldwide. Today, the platform holds over 80 billion euros in assets from&amp;nbsp;&lt;strong&gt;more than one million investors&lt;/strong&gt; which have accrued over 5 billion euros in returns.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;For further development and expansion of our successful business, Raisin is looking for a highly motivated, driven, and experienced &lt;strong&gt;Director of Engineering&lt;/strong&gt; to lead both strategically and operationally our Investment and Pension (IPP) teams (25+ engineers)&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This embraces high-quality conceptual and delivery performance of the teams, the health of the IPP engineering organization and system landscape,&amp;nbsp; an efficient and compliant development process, technical and business ownership of the Raisin’s IPP platform, and vendor relationships.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;At Raisin, we work in a domain driven organization with a binary-star leadership model. In this model, every Director of Engineering has a Product partner (Head of Product/ Director of Product).&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The Director Engineering (DE) leads both strategically and operationally across multiple cross-functional teams.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This embraces the six impact areas (in details below):&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Delivery quality and speed&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Domain ownership&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Team and culture&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Data strategy&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Process and compliance&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 18pt;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Your Responsibilities&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 12pt;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Delivery quality and speed&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;The DE is:&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;accountable for fulfilling the agreed team commitments to their Business-owners in time, scope, and budget&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;responsible for the performance of their teams&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;resolving impediments for their teams&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;nurturing a culture of accountability, pragmatism, and reusability&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;ensuring a strong delivery oriented collaboration between the different engineering teams&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;leading both complex technical and important business projects&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;leading internal software engineering projects and initiatives&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 12pt;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Domain ownership&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;The DE:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;drives long-term value creation for their domain&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;is fostering an environment of passion and fun for the business processes in their tribe&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;builds resilient domain expertise in their teams&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;has a deep understanding of the existing system landscape of their teams&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;collaborates closely with their Business Owner and other stakeholders&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;ensures Data Vendor management (evaluating, onboarding, and managing data-related vendors)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 12pt;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Tech Strategy&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;The DDE:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;shapes the technical strategy for their teams according to the Raisin&#39;s business needs&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;collaborates closely with other&amp;nbsp; Sr. Engineering Leads in shaping and implementing Raisin&#39;s Tech Strategy&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;actively initiates and contributes to strategic technical and architectural decisions&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;is always considering the strategic benefits and price of&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;keeping an existing technical solution&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;introducing a new alternative (e.g framework, tech stack, tooling, process)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 12pt;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Team and Culture&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;The DE is:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;fully responsible for the health, resilience high performance, and development of their teams&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;offering direct leadership of engineering leads and sometimes also tech leads as well&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;encouraging accountability, creativity, risk-taking, and ownership by delegating responsibility&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;attracting, hiring, and retaining diverse top technical talent for Raisin from around the world&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;proactively mentoring and coaching individual team members&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;ensuring a strong delivery-oriented collaboration between the different engineering teams&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;organizing workshops/hackathons&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;representing the company in external tech events advancing Raisin’s tech brand recognition&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;shaping and driving knowledge transfer best practices&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;nurturing and protecting our culture of trust&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;initiating, owning and nurturing tech initiatives (like guilds, workshops, regular meetups)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;recognizing high performance and rewarding accomplishments within their teams&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 12pt;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Process and Compliance&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;The DE:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;drives, improves, and applies existing Raisin standards and policies, Regulation and data privacy&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;contributes to an optimal toolchain with a high level of automation&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;develops, establishes, and continually improves documentation standards for the engineering organization&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;develops guidelines and best practices to ensure a lean software development process across different product teams&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;is responsible for the KPI-based reporting for their teams&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;actively monitors, analyses, and drives initiatives to continuously reduce their teams&#39; technical debt&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 18pt;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Your Profile&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You hold a university degree in Computer Science,&amp;nbsp; Engineering, Information Systems, or related fields or have equivalent practical experience&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Leadership experience 10y+. You are a senior engineering leader, across projects and teams, with a natural aptitude and passion for growing and developing high-performing teams&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;You have at least 4y experience in FinTech &lt;/strong&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Domain knowledge of Investment products is a strong advantage.&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Strong business mindset.&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong AWS knowledge, Java, SQL, Kafka/or other messaging solutions&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You are pragmatic and can handle the balance between both taking and delegating the lead in challenging situations&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You bring both strong strategic and excellent operational leadership skills&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You motivate and inspire by outstanding communication and interpersonal skills, both written and verbal, including communicating technical concepts to non-technical audiences&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You possess solid data engineering/analytics background and distinct hands-on mentality&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You are experienced with OKR and KPI-based target agreements&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You are familiar with architecturally-heavy systems, including designing, implementing, and evolving these system constraints&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You are fluent in English, knowledge of German or another European language would be a plus&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Join our mission, join our team – and grow with us!&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;At Raisin, we care about each other and it is one of our top priorities to foster an open and caring environment in which everyone feels welcome and comfortable. Our culture is strongly driven by our ambitious team, which connects more than 75 different nationalities.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As part of our team, you will benefit from:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Employee Development Budget of €2,000 and four full training days per year.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Flexible working hours, home office and 30 vacation days.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A company pension scheme (Betriebliche Altersvorsorge), which we support with 20%.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Enjoy more than 50+ different sports with Urban Sports Club: We subsidize your membership with more than €20 per month.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Do you miss being in the office? The Deutschland Ticket gets you there, which we subsidize with €25 per month.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Love cycling? With JobRad, lease the bike of your choice and enjoy tax savings, plus Raisin covers your monthly insurance costs.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Hungry all the time? Snacks, daily fresh fruit as well as drinks provided at the office.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You are moving from another country or city to join us? We may support your relocation.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.raisin.com/corporate/raisin-applicant-privacy-policy/&quot;&gt;&lt;em&gt;Raisin Applicant Privacy Policy&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p data-start=&quot;728&quot; data-end=&quot;900&quot;&gt;We value diversity and the unique experiences each individual brings. If you’re excited about this role but don’t meet every requirement, we still encourage you to apply.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p data-start=&quot;907&quot; data-end=&quot;1013&quot;&gt;We are an equal opportunity employer and are committed to creating an inclusive environment for everyone, regardless of race, colour, ancestry, religion, sex, national origin, sexual orientation, age, citizenship, marital status, disability, or gender identity.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;Find more English Speaking Jobs in Germany on Arbeitnow

&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;CSQ427R35&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As a Forward Deployed Engineer (FDE) you will work with customers to build and productionize solutions to their data &amp;amp; AI challenges using the Databricks platform. You will own the architecture, lead design decisions, and implement end-to-end systems spanning data engineering, AI, and application development. We work cross-functionally to shape long-term strategic priorities and initiatives alongside engineering, product, and developer relations. FDEs deliver with customer empathy, integrating with client systems, training, and other technical needs to help customers get most value out of their data.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This is a hands-on, customer-facing role for builders who thrive at the intersection of technology and business impact. The ideal candidate combines engineering expertise with adaptability, curiosity, and a passion for working with customers and teammates to solve complex problems that drive measurable outcomes. FDEs are billable and know how to complete projects according to specification with exceptional customer empathy.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;The impact you will have:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Production Solution Delivery: Lead impactful customer technical projects by delivering production-grade systems, designing and building reference architectures, custom applications and data ingestion and ML/AI model integration&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Transformational Impact: Guide strategic customers as they implement transformational big data projects including end-to-end design, build and deployment of industry-leading big data and AI applications. Work with engagement managers to scope technical delivery work with input from the customer&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Empower Customers: Guide customers on architecture and design; bootstrap or implement customer projects which leads to a customers&#39; successful understanding, evaluation and adoption of Databricks.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own the Architecture: Lead architecture and design decisions, ensuring solutions are secure, scalable, and aligned with both customer needs and Databricks best practices.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work with the Databricks technical team, Project Manager, Architect and Customer team to ensure the technical components of the engagement are delivered to meet customer&#39;s needs.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work with Engineering and Databricks Customer Support to provide product and implementation feedback and to guide rapid resolution for engagement specific product and support issues.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Customer Immersion: Embed with customer teams, engaging with stakeholders from technical ICs to executives to deeply understand challenges and deliver impact.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Reusable Assets &amp;amp; Scale: Contribute accelerators, frameworks, and best practices that scale impact across accounts and influence the Databricks product roadmap.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What we look for:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;6+ years experience in data engineering, data platforms &amp;amp; analytics, or software engineering&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Comfortable writing code in either Python, Scala, JavaScript/TypeScript, and modern frameworks&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Working knowledge of two or more common Cloud ecosystems (AWS, Azure, GCP) with expertise in at least one&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Deep experience with distributed computing with Apache Spark™ and knowledge of Spark runtime internals&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity with CI/CD for production deployments&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Working knowledge of MLOps, ML/AI models and AI APIs&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Design and deployment of performant production end-to-end data architectures and applications that combine data pipelines, ML/AI models, and user-facing interfaces.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with technical project delivery - managing scope, timelines and measurable outcomes, translating complex concepts into actionable solutions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Documentation and white-boarding skills.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience working with enterprise clients and managing conflicts across a broad stakeholder range&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build skills in technical areas, and demonstrate curiosity, adaptability, and eagerness to explore new technologies which support the deployment and integration of Databricks-based solutions to complete customer projects.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Travel to customers 20% of the time&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Databricks Certification&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About Databricks&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family: arial, sans-serif;&quot;&gt;Databricks is the Data and AI company. More than 20,000 organizations worldwide — including adidas, AT&amp;amp;T, Bayer, Block, Mastercard, Rivian, Unilever, and 70% of the Fortune 500 — rely on the Databricks Data + AI Platform to build and scale data and AI apps, analytics and agents. Headquartered in San Francisco with 30+ offices around the globe, Databricks offers a unified platform that includes Genie, Lakebase, Agent Bricks, Lakeflow, Lakehouse, and Unity Catalog. To learn more, follow Databricks on &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.linkedin.com/company/databricks&quot;&gt;LinkedIn&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a href=&quot;https://x.com/databricks&quot;&gt;X&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.youtube.com/@Databricks&quot;&gt;YouTube&lt;/a&gt;, and &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.instagram.com/databricksinc/?hl=en&quot;&gt;Instagram&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Benefits&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/span&gt;At Databricks, we strive to provide comprehensive benefits and perks that meet the needs of all of our employees. For specific details on the benefits offered in your region click &lt;a href=&quot;https://docs.google.com/document/d/154un3e8Xav4BceOSlcYFZRGEuQI54xMxVydRwQn54eQ/edit?usp=sharing&quot;&gt;here&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Our Commitment to Diversity and Inclusion&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;At Databricks, we are committed to fostering a diverse and inclusive culture where everyone can excel. We take great care to ensure that our hiring practices are inclusive and meet equal employment opportunity standards. Individuals looking for employment at Databricks are considered without regard to age, color, disability, ethnicity, family or marital status, gender identity or expression, language, national origin, physical and mental ability, political affiliation, race, religion, sexual orientation, socio-economic status, veteran status, and other protected characteristics.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Compliance&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;If access to export-controlled technology or source code is required for performance of job duties, it is within Employer&#39;s discretion whether to apply for a U.S. government license for such positions, and Employer may decline to proceed with an applicant on this basis alone.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;Find Jobs in Germany on Arbeitnow

&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 10pt;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;SLSQ427R368&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;While candidates in the listed locations are encouraged for this role, we are open to remote candidates in other locations.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;This senior leadership role&lt;/strong&gt; will lead Partner Sales for the&amp;nbsp; Central EMEA region (Germany. CH, Austria eastern Europe), focused on consulting and Systems Integrator (C&amp;amp;SI) partners, as a member of the Regional Leadership Team. The regional leader will build the regional ecosystem strategy and plan aligned with regional and functional priorities.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Your direct reports will include Partner Sales managers/directors in the region. You will report to the Vice President, EMEA Alliances.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As Director, Partner Sales, you own the partner go-to-market strategy for the assigned region — driving co-sell motions in our top accounts, working with priority partners for co-sell and co-deliver, building durable pipelines, and holding partners accountable to execution that converts to partner-sourced and partner-influenced consumption.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This is a highly visible, strategic role: you drive the partner-first motion across Sales, Field Engineering, Marketing, and work with the extended team of Partner Solution Architects, Partner Marketing, Partner Management and Partner Enablement. You carry Databricks&#39; regional partner narrative to senior partner executives in our partner ecosystem. You will own and grow executive relationships and commitment with strategic partners across the region — including global and regional systems integrators (e.g. Accenture, Deloitte, Capgemini) and specialist data and AI partners — and you bring deep industry knowledge and an operator&#39;s mindset powered by modern AI tooling.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p data-renderer-start-pos=&quot;2006&quot;&gt;&lt;strong data-renderer-mark=&quot;true&quot;&gt;The impact you will have: &lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Leadership &amp;amp; Team Development&lt;/strong&gt; — Lead the regional Alliances/C&amp;amp;SI function, building and developing a high-performing cross-functional team while representing the partner organisation in regional leadership forums.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Strategic Planning &amp;amp; Ecosystem Leadership&lt;/strong&gt; — Own the multi-year regional partner territory plan — forming a compelling 3-year vision with partner segmentation, coverage model, and operational rhythm aligned to regional and functional priorities.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Executive Relationships &amp;amp; Narrative&lt;/strong&gt; — Own executive-level partner relationships, building joint business plans and executive-ready narratives that represent Databricks credibly to senior partner and customer leadership.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Account-Level Co-Sell &amp;amp; Big Bet Workshops&lt;/strong&gt; — Drive joint account planning workshops in Top/must-win accounts with priority partners as the primary co-sell and pipeline creation mechanism; coach AEs and scale the partner motion through the field.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Pipeline &amp;amp; Revenue Engine&lt;/strong&gt; — Architect the regional partner GTM strategy and convert it into a tangible, partner-sourced and partner-influenced pipeline and consumption. Drive partner-led demand generation at scale — industry events, co-funded campaigns, partner pitch days, and regional kickoff sponsorships.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Product-Specific Partner GTM&lt;/strong&gt; — Own product-specific partner campaigns (Migration &amp;amp; Modernisation, Genie, Lakebase, AgentBricks) aligned to platform priorities; proactively build partner capability on new products to maintain delivery coverage as the product mix evolves.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Partner Execution &amp;amp; Accountability&lt;/strong&gt; — Hold strategic SI partners and tiered programme partners (Gold/Silver) to joint commitments on both delivery capability and business development; run a disciplined operating cadence of pipeline reviews, forecast, and KPI inspection anchored to Salesforce; report impact, not activity.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Partner Delivery Quality&lt;/strong&gt; — Own partner delivery quality governance — resolve escalations, ensure partners&#39; staff to SoW, and work with FDE/Field Engineering on delivery models that protect customer outcomes.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Cross-Functional Orchestration &amp;amp; Field Adoption&lt;/strong&gt; — Set direction across Sales, Field Engineering, Marketing, and Partner Solution Architecture; embed partner strategy into territory reviews and drive internal field adoption so AEs actively engage partners in their accounts.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Solution Development &amp;amp; Delivery Readiness&lt;/strong&gt; — Co-create differentiated, industry-specific joint solutions and repeatable GTM campaigns while supporting SI partner practice development through enablement, asset development, and delivery excellence.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;AI-Driven Operations&lt;/strong&gt; — Use AI tools as the primary operating system for pipeline inspection, partner intelligence, exec meeting prep, and partner-facing demos; drive AI fluency across the partner ecosystem.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p data-renderer-start-pos=&quot;2367&quot;&gt;&lt;strong data-renderer-mark=&quot;true&quot;&gt;What we look for:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Leadership Experience&lt;/strong&gt; — Proven people leader who has built and scaled teams of partner sales directors/managers, operating as a member of a partner or regional leadership team in a leading software company.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Partner/Alliance Sales Experience&lt;/strong&gt; — Extensive experience in partner/alliance sales, channel, or GTM at an enterprise software, cloud, or data company with a proven track record of building partner-sourced pipeline and driving measurable revenue impact.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;SI &amp;amp; Executive Engagement&lt;/strong&gt; — Specific experience working with Global and Regional Systems Integrators at an executive level to lead industry GTM activation, CXO engagement, and transformational outcomes.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Account-Level Co-Sell Execution&lt;/strong&gt; — Demonstrated ability to drive joint account planning workshops with SI partners in enterprise accounts, translating partner capability into sourced pipeline and closed consumption.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Cross-Functional Leadership &amp;amp; Field Influence&lt;/strong&gt; — Track record leading across Sales, Field/Technical, Marketing, Cloud partners (AWS, Azure, GCP), and SI/ISV partners in a matrixed environment; proven ability to embed partner strategy into field operating rhythms and influence AEs without direct authority.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Executive Presence&lt;/strong&gt; — Shapes a compelling business narrative and aligns senior internal, partner, and customer stakeholders; represents Databricks credibly at the CXO level.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Operational Rigour&lt;/strong&gt; — Clean pipeline hygiene, KPI discipline, and data-driven inspection; comfort defining and running OKRs that drive predictability in partner-sourced pipeline.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Partner Delivery Governance&lt;/strong&gt; — Experience managing partner delivery quality — resolving escalations, holding partners to SoW commitments, and working with professional services on co-delivery models.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Industry &amp;amp; Domain Expertise&lt;/strong&gt; — Deep knowledge of SI business models, industry workflows, and regional buying patterns; understands how data and AI create value and translates use cases into joint partner solutions.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;AI Fluency &amp;amp; Travel&lt;/strong&gt; — Fluency with modern AI productivity tools, including AI-powered analytics for pipeline and partner intelligence; ability to travel 25–40% for partner business reviews, account-planning workshops, and executive engagements.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About Databricks&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family: arial, sans-serif;&quot;&gt;Databricks is the Data and AI company. More than 20,000 organizations worldwide — including adidas, AT&amp;amp;T, Bayer, Block, Mastercard, Rivian, Unilever, and 70% of the Fortune 500 — rely on the Databricks Data + AI Platform to build and scale data and AI apps, analytics and agents. Headquartered in San Francisco with 30+ offices around the globe, Databricks offers a unified platform that includes Genie, Lakebase, Agent Bricks, Lakeflow, Lakehouse, and Unity Catalog. To learn more, follow Databricks on &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.linkedin.com/company/databricks&quot;&gt;LinkedIn&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a href=&quot;https://x.com/databricks&quot;&gt;X&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.youtube.com/@Databricks&quot;&gt;YouTube&lt;/a&gt;, and &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.instagram.com/databricksinc/?hl=en&quot;&gt;Instagram&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Benefits&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/span&gt;At Databricks, we strive to provide comprehensive benefits and perks that meet the needs of all of our employees. For specific details on the benefits offered in your region click &lt;a href=&quot;https://docs.google.com/document/d/154un3e8Xav4BceOSlcYFZRGEuQI54xMxVydRwQn54eQ/edit?usp=sharing&quot;&gt;here&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Our Commitment to Diversity and Inclusion&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;At Databricks, we are committed to fostering a diverse and inclusive culture where everyone can excel. We take great care to ensure that our hiring practices are inclusive and meet equal employment opportunity standards. Individuals looking for employment at Databricks are considered without regard to age, color, disability, ethnicity, family or marital status, gender identity or expression, language, national origin, physical and mental ability, political affiliation, race, religion, sexual orientation, socio-economic status, veteran status, and other protected characteristics.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Compliance&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;If access to export-controlled technology or source code is required for performance of job duties, it is within Employer&#39;s discretion whether to apply for a U.S. government license for such positions, and Employer may decline to proceed with an applicant on this basis alone.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;Find Jobs in Germany on Arbeitnow

&lt;p&gt;We are looking for a&amp;nbsp;&lt;strong&gt;Senior Data Platform Engineer&lt;/strong&gt; to join the &lt;strong&gt;Data Platform&lt;/strong&gt; at Smartly!&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Smartly is building the standard path for governed data sharing across product services, analytics, and AI/ML. The Data Platform team owns the contracts, control mechanisms, publication paths, catalog metadata, lifecycle rules, lineage, permissions, and runtime building blocks that make reusable data safe and practical at scale.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This is a role for someone who wants to shape a platform early, while working on concrete production problems from the start. Smartly already has the production systems, Kafka backbone, PostgreSQL databases, analytical consumers, and AI/ML use cases that need a better data foundation. The challenge is to turn that reality into a standard path that engineers actually want to use.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Our first milestone is focused: centrally managed publishing tables in service-owned PostgreSQL databases, captured through Debezium CDC into Kafka, and registered in DataHub with ownership, lifecycle, lineage, and impact-analysis metadata. Longer-term, the platform expands toward self-service data products, governed materialisations, durable shared state, and reusable data across Smartly’s operational and analytical systems.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This is not a role where you only maintain an existing reporting pipeline. You will help design and build the platform path that other engineering teams use when they publish and consume shared data.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;What you will do&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Design and build platform services, tools, and workflows for contract-driven data publishing and consumption.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build the first production path for platform-managed PostgreSQL publishing tables, Debezium CDC, Kafka topics, and catalog registration.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Create GitOps-style workflows where contracts, schemas, ownership, lifecycle, compatibility, policy metadata, and runtime desired state are reviewed, validated, and reconciled as code.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build tooling that gives product engineers fast feedback before they publish or change data products.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Help define how Smartly models data products, publishing contracts, schema evolution, field stability, deletion semantics, access policy, lineage, and cost attribution.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Operate and improve the CDC runtime model, including Kubernetes workloads, source-specific isolation, offsets, schema history, heartbeats, signal channels, lag visibility, replay, resnapshotting, and recovery.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Integrate platform metadata into DataHub so engineers can discover data products, understand ownership, trace lineage, and reason about the impact of changes.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work with product, infrastructure, data engineering, analytics, and AI/ML teams to make the standard path easier and safer than bespoke point-to-point integrations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;What we are looking for&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong experience building and operating production software systems, preferably in platform, infrastructure, backend, or data-intensive environments.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Deep understanding of distributed systems trade-offs: reliability, idempotency, replay, eventual consistency, ownership boundaries, compatibility, and operational failure modes.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Practical experience with PostgreSQL or other relational databases, including schema design, migrations, transactions, replication, or operational performance.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with Kafka, event streaming, CDC, Debezium, or adjacent data-movement technologies. Direct Debezium experience is valuable, but strong fundamentals matter more.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience building software that other engineers use: CLIs, internal platforms, control planes, automation, CI validation, developer tooling, or self-service workflows.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity with Kubernetes and cloud or infrastructure platforms, including runtime isolation, deployment, observability, and operational ownership.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to turn ambiguous architectural direction into practical increments, make trade-offs explicit, and deliver useful production systems without waiting for perfect certainty.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Clear written and spoken communication in English. This role involves aligning multiple engineering teams around standards, contracts, and ownership boundaries.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;Useful experience, but not required&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;DataHub or other data catalog, lineage, or governance systems.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Open table formats such as Apache Iceberg, object-store-backed data lakes, S3, BigQuery, ClickHouse, or analytical storage systems.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;GitHub Actions, policy-as-code, infrastructure-as-code, controllers, operators, or reconciliation-based systems.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Data contracts, schema registries, Protobuf, Avro, JSON Schema, compatibility checking, field-level metadata, or contract testing.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience supporting analytics, AI/ML, feature-store-style access patterns, or cross-domain product-service integrations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with JVM languages and Python, TypeScript, Go, or Ruby.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;What we offer you&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;At Smartly, we offer a place where you can do meaningful technical work while growing with a global team.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Inclusive global culture built on trust, transparency, open feedback, and respect for different perspectives.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Global impact through technology used by major brands to plan, create, optimize, and understand digital advertising at scale.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Wellbeing support, paid holidays, family leave, and sustainable ways of working.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Equity options, performance-based rewards, competitive compensation, and career development opportunities.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A flexible hybrid workplace that balances office collaboration with focused remote work. At Smartly we work 3 days a week from the office.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;About Smartly&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Smartly is an advertising technology company helping brands create, manage, optimize, and understand digital advertising across major media platforms. Our engineering organization builds the systems that connect media, creative, and intelligence capabilities into a product used by customers globally.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We value clear communication, ownership, curiosity, and collaboration across teams. We want Smartly to be a place where people can do strong work, grow, and feel respected.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Not sure you tick every box? Please apply anyway. We care about strong engineering fundamentals, ownership, curiosity, and the ability to build reliable systems with others. Direct experience with every technology listed here is less important than the judgment to learn, reason from first principles, and ship useful platform capabilities.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About Smartly&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Smartly is the AI-powered advertising technology company transforming ad experiences for brands and their consumers. Our comprehensive advertising platform seamlessly integrates the capabilities of media, creative, and intelligence to power more than 800 billion impressions and generate more than 300 billion creatives annually, delivering tangible business outcomes for brands and advertisers.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Smartly is the only company in the industry recognized as a Leader in The Forrester Wave: Creative Advertising Technologies with PwC validating the results it delivers for brands. We manage creative and media for 700+ brands worldwide and $6B in ad spend across the largest media platforms, including Facebook, Google, Instagram, Pinterest, Snap, and TikTok. Our end-to-end technology, unmatched access to media platforms and exceptional customer service help Fortune 500 brands to reach and engage consumers and learn what performs best.Smartly is a multinational and diverse team of 750+ Smartlies from 60+ nationalities, working in 13 countries. Together, we want to create and maintain an inclusive environment where everyone feels respected and heard. Our Diversity, Equity &amp;amp; Inclusion approach is at the heart of it.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Visit &lt;a class=&quot;c-link c-link--underline&quot; href=&quot;http://smartly.io/&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot; data-stringify-link=&quot;http://Smartly.io&quot; data-sk=&quot;tooltip_parent&quot;&gt;Smartly&lt;/a&gt; to learn more.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;The processing of your information is described in our &lt;a href=&quot;https://cdn.prod.website-files.com/67ed4ab7f914accf87aa070c/698a11cb716926c1d76c1641_Smartly.io%20Group%20-%20Privacy%20Notice%20for%20Candidates%20-%201_2026.pdf&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;Candidate Privacy Notice&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;Find Jobs in Germany on Arbeitnow

&lt;div class=&quot;gmail_default&quot; style=&quot;font-size: small;&quot;&gt;
&lt;div&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Why Mozilla?&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Mozilla Corporation is the non-profit-backed technology company that has shaped the internet for the better over the last 25 years. We make pioneering brands like Firefox, the privacy-minded web browser, and Pocket, a service for keeping up with the best content online. Now, with more than 225 million people around the world using our products each month, we’re shaping the next 25 years of technology and helping to reclaim an internet built for people, not companies. Our work focuses on diverse areas including AI, social media, security and more. And we’re doing this while never losing our focus on our core mission – to make the internet better for people.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;The Mozilla Corporation is wholly owned by the non-profit 501(c) Mozilla Foundation. This means we aren’t beholden to any shareholders - only to our mission. Along with thousands of volunteer contributors and collaborators all over the world, Mozillians design, build and distribute &lt;/span&gt;&lt;strong&gt;open-source&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt; software that enables people to enjoy the internet on their terms.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About this team and role:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;We’re looking for a hands-on Mobile Product Manager with a primary focus on Firefox for iOS, while also contributing across mobile (including Android).&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;This role is about building a better browser, turning downloads into loyal users, and creating experiences that truly stand out. If you’ve shipped mobile apps, obsess over details that improve everyday use, and love turning user insights into real improvements, this is a great opportunity to drive impact at Firefox.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you’ll do:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Build a fundamentally better browser experience: fix bugs, refine UI and navigation, improve downloads, menus, performance, and all the small details that make Firefox noticeably better for users who care about privacy, quality and reliability.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Drive strong activation and retention: focus on the new-user journey, quickly hooking people after they install the app, understanding where they drop off, and relentlessly optimizing the funnel through data, testing and iteration.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Deliver differentiating features and experiences that make Firefox stickier for key user groups, the kinds of things others can’t or won’t build.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Work closely with engineers, designers, data science and TPMs to ship high-impact improvements while balancing user needs, technical constraints, privacy and performance goals.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Stay deeply connected to real users: track App Store trends and discussions, test apps hands-on, analyze reviews and analytics, and turn those insights into concrete enhancements for Firefox on iOS and Android.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Monitor app health in App Store Connect and Google Play Console (crashes, ANRs, ratings) and support acquisition/retention efforts through ASO, store listings and growth experiments.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Adapt and optimize Firefox for global markets (Europe, Japan, Asia etc.), keeping cultural differences and local realities like data constraints in mind.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you&#39;ll bring:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
